author of a document highlighting the importance of oral hygiene, further emphasizing her commitment to patient care and health education. Her research contributions are significant in enhancing the understanding and management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, showcasing her expertise and dedication to improving patient outcomes in this area.", "JULIÁN FERNÁNDEZ MACÍAS:Julián Fernández Macías is a multifaceted professional involved in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia. He is a contributor to a manual that addresses this condition, specifically focusing on solutions applicable in hospital settings. In addition to his contributions to medical literature, he works as a cook in the Hospital's Kitchen Service, where he plays a vital role in the Functional Unit of Orofaríngea Dysphagia. Furthermore, Julián is an author of recipes featured in Cocina Hospitalaria, showcasing his culinary expertise and commitment to enhancing the dietary options for patients with dysphagia. Through these roles, Julián Fernández Macías combines his knowledge of dysphagia with practical culinary skills to improve patient care in a hospital environment.", "PILAR GALLEGO IZQUIERDO:Pilar Gallego Izquierdo is a speech therapist working in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias, where she specializes in dysphagia, particularly oropharyngeal dysphagia. She is a contributor to a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a specific focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Additionally, Pilar Gallego Izquierdo is recognized as an author who has made significant contributions to the understanding of oropharyngeal dysphagia, enhancing the knowledge and resources available in this field.", "ELISA GARCÍA GARCÍA:Elisa García García is a Nursing Auxiliary Technician in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. In addition to her role in clinical nutrition, she is also a co-author of a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia, which emphasizes dietary adaptations for patients suffering from this condition.", "ANTONIO GIL CORDERO:Antonio Gil Cordero is a prominent figure in the field of dietary management and culinary services within healthcare. He is a co-author of a manual on oropharyngeal dysphagia, which enhances the understanding of dietary needs for individuals with swallowing difficulties. Additionally, he has contributed recipes to \"Cocina Hospitalaria,\" showcasing his expertise in hospital cuisine. Currently, Antonio serves as the Head of Kitchen at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias, where he is responsible for managing food services for patients, ensuring that their dietary requirements are met with professionalism and care.", "NURIA GIL-FOURNIER ESQUERRA:Nuria Gil-Fournier Esquerra is a Specialist Physician in the Endocrinology and Nutrition Section at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She also practices at the Hospital General de Villalba in Madrid, where she specializes in endocrinology and nutrition. In addition to her clinical work, Nuria is a contributor to clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in this area, which is closely related to otolaryngology. She works in the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea, where she is actively involved in the treatment of patients with dysphagia. Furthermore, Nuria is a researcher focused on dysphagia screening methods and clinical assessments, and she explores the intersection of internet technology and health, particularly in relation to dysphagia.", "CARMEN GÓMEZ TRIGUERO:Carmen Gómez Triguero is a Specialist Physician in the Rehabilitation Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She is actively involved in research concerning oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, contributing as a co-author to various studies in this field. Additionally, she has played a significant role in developing a manual that addresses solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, with a particular focus on exercises designed for orofacial structures that are crucial for the swallowing process. Through her work, Carmen Gómez Triguero has established herself as a key contributor to the understanding and treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia.", "MONTSERRAT MARTÍNEZ LIÉBANA:Montserrat Martínez Liébana is a Senior Technician in Dietetics and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias.", "LOURDES MONEVA VICENTE:Lourdes Moneva Vicente is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She specializes in the nutritional treatment of oropharyngeal dysphagia, providing essential nursing care for patients affected by this condition. In addition to her clinical work, Lourdes is also a co-author of a document that emphasizes the importance of oral hygiene, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care and outcomes in her field.", "NATASHA PÉREZ MARRERO:Natasha Pérez Marrero is a Specialist Physician in the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. She is recognized for her contributions to the clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her expertise in the field of otolaryngology.", "TERESA RIVERA RODRÍGUEZ:Teresa Rivera Rodríguez is a prominent figure in the field of otolaryngology, serving as the Head of the Otolaryngology Service at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. In addition to her leadership role, she is also an Associate Professor of Health Sciences. Her expertise is further demonstrated through her contributions to clinical guidelines on dysphagia, indicating her significant involvement and knowledge in this specialized area of medicine.", "MANUAL DE DISFAGIA OROFARÍNGEA:The \"Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea\" is a comprehensive guide designed to address oropharyngeal dysphagia through a multidisciplinary approach. It offers a wide range of solutions for the assessment, diagnosis, and treatment of this swallowing disorder, focusing on various aspects such as hydration, nutritional therapy, dietary adaptations, and rehabilitation strategies.\n\nThe manual includes detailed information on diagnostic scales and evaluation techniques for swallowing disorders, as well as clinical history considerations, gastrointestinal symptoms, and functional capacity assessments. It emphasizes the importance of tailored dietary recommendations, including texture modifications and liquid viscosities, to meet the nutritional needs of individuals with oropharyngeal dysphagia.\n\nIn addition to dietary guidelines, the manual provides practical solutions such as recipes and cooking techniques specifically designed for patients with swallowing difficulties. It also discusses exercises and techniques aimed at improving muscle strength and swallowing function, particularly for those affected by neurological conditions, head and neck cancer, or post-stroke recovery.\n\nFurthermore, the \"Manual de Disfagia Orofaringea\" addresses safety protocols in food preparation, allergen management, and oral hygiene practices, ensuring comprehensive care for patients. It serves as a valuable resource for healthcare professionals and caregivers involved in the management of oropharyngeal dysphagia, particularly in elderly patients and those with complex medical needs.", "VIRGINIA RODRÍGUEZ CAMPUZANO:Virginia Rodríguez Campuzano is a dedicated nurse in the Clinical Nutrition and Dietetics Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias, where she specializes in the care of patients with oropharyngeal dysphagia. In her role, she is actively involved in providing nursing care tailored to the needs of these patients. Additionally, Virginia has contributed to the field through her research on multidisciplinary solutions for oropharyngeal dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to advancing knowledge and practices in this area. She is also a co-author of a document emphasizing the importance of oral hygiene, further showcasing her dedication to improving patient care and health outcomes.", "MANUEL RODRÍGUEZ PARADINAS:Manuel Rodríguez Paradinas is a prominent figure in the field of oropharyngeal dysphagia rehabilitation, serving as a co-author and contributor to clinical guidelines related to dysphagia. He is recognized as an expert in otolaryngology and plays a vital role in the multidisciplinary team at the Unidad Funcional de Disfagia Orofaríngea. His research interests include studying the impact of digital technology on health and dysphagia, highlighting his commitment to advancing knowledge in this area. Additionally, he specializes in the Otolaryngology Service and is responsible for overseeing the Oropharyngeal Dysphagia Functional Unit at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. Through his work, Manuel Rodríguez Paradinas focuses on the treatment and evaluation of oropharyngeal dysphagia, contributing significantly to the understanding and management of this condition.", "PAULA ROMERO CORTÉS:Paula Romero Cortés is a medical resident specializing in Endocrinology and Nutrition at the Hospital Universitario Príncipe de Asturias. In addition to her clinical training, she is also an author who contributes to the understanding of nutritional support for patients with dysphagia, highlighting her commitment to improving patient care through both practice and research."], "parameters": {"model": "text-embedding-3-small", "temperature": 0.0, "frequency_penalty": null, "presence_penalty": null, "top_p": 1.0, "max_tokens": 4000, "n": 1}, "history": null}